# Normalize everything to LF in the repository. The _wsl/*.sh scripts run under
# Ubuntu and break outright if they are checked out with CRLF endings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Patches must survive byte-for-byte or `git apply` rejects them.
*.patch -text

# ngspice netlists and generated run output are read by Linux tooling.
*.cir text eol=lf
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.py  text eol=lf

# Append-only store tables (lna/datastore.py) and the playbook edge log
# (lna/playbook.py) are combined ACROSS git lines (main/lna-data vs engineer)
# only through lna/sync_lines.py (plans2/15-ENGINEER-PROPOSAL.md SS5.6), never
# through a git merge/rebase of these files directly. Reason: git's line-based
# text merge can reorder, interleave, or duplicate independently-appended
# JSONL lines across a 3-way merge, and datastore.py's snapshots pin an exact
# (line count, sha256-of-byte-prefix) -- a merge that changes so much as one
# byte's position anywhere in the pinned prefix makes every existing snapshot
# for that table permanently unverifiable (datastore.load raises on the
# mismatch). `-merge -diff` disables git's content merge and content diff for
# these paths so a conflicting cross-line merge fails loudly (a real git
# conflict marker) instead of silently interleaving; the actual cross-line
# combination path is always `python lna/sync_lines.py --source ... --dest ...`.
lna/data/*.jsonl        -merge -diff
lna/playbook/edges.jsonl -merge -diff
